SUMMARY:Laser Cutter Safety Training
DESCRIPTION:Noisebridge Hackerspace Learn how to be safe while using the laser cutter! We have a 150W\, CO2 laser cutter with a 3 x 4 ft bed. This training is required to use the laser cutter because we don't want people setting our most expensive equipment donation on fire. You have to do this training even if you were trained at the old space\, as we have different safety features now. Training covers * Dangers of the laser cutter * How to be safe * How to put out a fire Each participant will cut a piece of cardboard on the laser cutter while following all the safety steps. This is also a good place to ask questions about specific materials or projects. There is a 5$ fee to register\, and we suggest a 20-30$ donation for this class: https://donate.noisebridge.net. If the registration fee is a barrier to your participation\, please reach out to the event organisers. | Source: DC415 San Francisco | Tags: security | https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/316160300/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/316160300/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4108446adb15d4c1@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260831T160009Z
DTSTART:20260907T180000Z
DTEND:20260907T210000Z
SUMMARY:Woodworking Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Noisebridge Hackerspace -please read the whole updated description!- Come to work on your own projects and get some feedback from your fellow woodchucks. We have a planer\, drill presses\, hand tools\, a table saw\, and much more! ###################### **starting June 8 we will be taking a break from the intensive power tool trainings provided in previous sessions.** For the next few weeks we want to use wood night as a time for actively working on projects and designing ideas for your projects. Happy to help with some guided use of the tools\, but for now no full training will be offered. If you are new to the woodshop you are still welcome to join\, just know that we will not provide a full training on the tools. If you have significant experience using a Tablesaw\, mitre saw\, planer etc then this should not be an issue. We do have some scrap wood available\, but bringing some wood for your project\, especially if it is larger or more crafty\, is highly encouraged. We recommend getting your wood at Lowe’s (cheaper) Discount builders supply (closer to NB) or Beronio (higher quality and carry lots of hardwoods). Please feel free to ask questions on the discord if you are unsure about what to get for your project. | Source: DC415 San Francisco | Tags: security | https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/316176131/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/316176131/
END:VEVENT
