SUMMARY:Chicago fireboat tour with Scanner
DESCRIPTION:<b>What is it?</b><br>Join the <a href="http://scanner.dev" target="_blank">Scanner team</a> and the security community after Blue Team Con wraps for the day for a Chicago fireboat tour\, cruising Lake Michigan and the Chicago River as the skyline rolls by.<br><br>The boat itself spent decades on Chicago's Fire Department fleet and still carries the photos\, artifacts\, and equipment from that life on board as a working piece of the city's firefighting history. Grab a spot on deck alongside our team and hear how a stretch of river that used to be stockyards and warehouses became the restaurants\, towers\, and riverwalk you see today.<br><br>The tour runs for 2 hours. Please arrive by 5:15pm. The boat leaves right at 5:30pm and cannot wait\, so build in extra time to get from the conference to the harbor.<br><br><b>Who can attend?</b><br>The event is intended for active security practitioner and leaders. All registrations are subject to review. Space is limited and all registrations require approval. Please register via the Luma link above. | Source: Chicago InfoSec Events Calendar | Tags: infosec\, security | http://scanner.dev"
LOCATION:https://luma.com/c8o2w6gw
URL:http://scanner.dev"
END:VEVENT
